ays  since you first came out with it wow  that's impressive because i've been  doing this for years  but i've never asked a question you've  never asked a question and you've been  watching for years  listen guys if you watch my q a sundays  every week and you've never asked a  question  today is the day to break that pattern  and ask your questions all right let's  see what hussein has to say  when you're buying a property that is  strictly a cash purchase  and it's not mortgageable is it possible  to do an option agreement with the  vendor  to do the bare minimum to just make it  mortgageable say no kitchen or bathroom  and just put a used one in  and then sell it at a much higher price  and then keep the difference so that  when we put it back on the market  there's still enough profit for someone  else to come in  and do it up to an excellent standard  for example  a property selling for 150 000 pounds  cash purchase  and value 230. so we come and do a  little bit of work and put it on the  market for 175  and now it's mortgageable this way we  put in a little bit of money just to  make it mortgageable and then sell it  onto an investor which will do the full  refurb  um yeah that is possible that is very  possible in fact that's something that  um myself and my wife have done  uh many times we've bought a property  that's completely run down and instead  of doing it all up to a really high  standard  we've just fixed the kitchen and  bathroom and then sold it  so it is possible you can also do with  an option agreement  as well so yeah you can do that my  friend  okay last question okay so get  commenting folks let's see your  questions  ajaz b says right 75k available to spend  equity was released from my hand do i go  down the hmo route or buy two or three  properties on the buy to let mortgages  and pull it all down on a derelict or  put it all down on a dairy property  also in my city of nottingham not many  properties available in my price bracket  would 